{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "GEOSFP",
    "description": "GEOS-FP regridding model — the coupler half of the geosfp loader+regridding-model split (RFC pure-io-data-loaders §6/§7; bead esm-3nc.2, following the esm-3nc.1 era5/wrf pattern). Exposes NASA GMAO GEOS-FP assimilated meteorology (0.25°×0.3125° global, GEOS-Chem 72-level) on the simulation's target grid for coupling into EarthSciML systems.\n\nStructure (RFC §6): it declares the six pure-I/O GEOS-FP grid loaders as subsystems under their original names (GEOSFP_A1/A3cld/A3dyn/A3mstC/A3mstE/I3 → ./geosfp_<coll>_loader.esm), so loader fields are referenced as GEOSFP.<coll>.<var> and re-exposed as model observeds (GEOSFP.T, GEOSFP.U, …). Native grids are geographic (longlat/WGS84) → longlat identity reprojection (esd-47z.1). Regridding is per-variable (`regrid`): A3dyn staggered winds U/V/OMEGA → B-spline (esd-47z.3); all other fields → conservative. The hybrid sigma-pressure Ap/Bp tables (former GEOSFP_hybrid_coefs kind:lookup, removed in the 0.6.0 hard break) are now the top-level function_tables geosfp_Ap_pa and geosfp_Bp, consumed by P = Ap(lev)+Bp(lev)·PS.\n\nDerived observeds on the target grid: pressure P, virtual temperature Tv and Tv_sfc, layer-mean virtual temperature Tv_bar, and the lat/lon coordinate metrics δxδlon, δyδlat. MeanWind coupling: GEOSFP.U/V/OMEGA → MeanWind v_lon/v_lat/v_lev.\n\nMigrated from EarthSciData.jl@830435a065f27e99f10bba91107ca1730322cc6b:src/geosfp.jl:410 (GEOSFP constructor, esm-1c6s); split into pure loaders + regridding model by esm-3nc.2.",
    "tags": [
      "earthsci_data",
      "meteorology",
      "atmospheric_dynamics",
      "data_loader",
      "geos_fp",
      "global",
      "hybrid_pressure",
      "geos_chem",
      "nasa",
      "regridding_model",
      "longlat",
      "pure-io-split"
    ],
    "created": "2026-05-30T00:00:00Z",
    "authors": [
      "NASA GMAO / GEOS-Chem",
      "EarthSciModels migration (esm-3nc.2)"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "GEOS-FP data archived for GEOS-Chem classic. NASA Global Modeling and Assimilation Office (GMAO). AWS S3 mirror: s3://geos-chem/GEOS_{domain}/GEOS_FP/. See http://geoschemdata.wustl.edu/ExtData/ for current domain and file-type options.",
        "url": "http://geoschemdata.wustl.edu/ExtData/"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Molod, A., Takacs, L., Suarez, M., and Bacmeister, J. (2015). Development of the GEOS-5 atmospheric general circulation model: evolution from MERRA to MERRA2. Geosci. Model Dev., 8, 1339–1356.",
        "doi": "10.5194/gmd-8-1339-2015"
      },
      {
        "citation": "GEOS-Chem vertical grid documentation: https://wiki.seas.harvard.edu/geos-chem/index.php/GEOS-Chem_vertical_grids",
        "url": "https://wiki.seas.harvard.edu/geos-chem/index.php/GEOS-Chem_vertical_grids"
      },
      {
        "citation": "Source: EarthSciData.jl@830435a065f27e99f10bba91107ca1730322cc6b:src/geosfp.jl (GEOSFPFileSet, GEOSFP constructor, Ap/Bp hybrid grid coefficients, geosfp_staggering). Test: test/geosfp_test.jl. Docs: docs present in pinned commit."
      }
    ]
  },
  "models": {
    "GEOSFP": {
      "reference": {
        "notes": "This is the regridding-model half of the pure-IO loader migration (RFC pure-io-data-loaders §6/§7; esm-3nc.1 era5/wrf pattern, bead esm-3nc.2). The pre-migration geosfp.esm carried both the GEOSFP coupler model AND seven co-located data_loaders blocks (six grid loaders GEOSFP_A1/A3cld/A3dyn/A3mstC/A3mstE/I3 plus a GEOSFP_hybrid_coefs kind:lookup table). The six grid loaders are now pure-I/O files referenced as subsystems under their ORIGINAL names (GEOSFP_A1 … GEOSFP_I3 → ./geosfp_<coll>_loader.esm), so every observed expression GEOSFP_<coll>.<var> keeps resolving unchanged. The GEOSFP_hybrid_coefs lookup became the top-level function_tables geosfp_Ap_pa and geosfp_Bp (kind:lookup is no longer a valid DataLoader kind in esm 0.6.0).\n\nReprojection (RFC §6 step 2): every loader's grid.crs.projection is 'longlat' (geographic WGS84), so the reprojection rule selected by convention is ESD reprojection/longlat.esm (esd-47z.1) — the IDENTITY transform (a no-op for an unprojected grid).\n\nRegridding (RFC §6 step 3 / §5.2): declared per variable in the model `regrid` block. The A3dyn C-grid wind components U (x-edge), V (y-edge), OMEGA (z-edge interface) are staggered → B-spline interpolating regridder (ESD regridding/bspline_regrid.esm, esd-47z.3); every other consumed loader field (all A1/A3cld/A3mstC/A3mstE/I3 fields and A3dyn RH/DTRAIN) is cell-centered → conservative area-weighted overlap join (ESD regridding/conservative_regrid_overlap_join.esm). OMEGA's upstream zero-extrapolation (extrapolate_type=0.0) has no schema field and is documented in the A3dyn loader metadata.\n\nMeanWind coupling: the re-exposed top-level GEOSFP.U/V/OMEGA observeds preserve the couple2 contract (GEOSFP.U/V/OMEGA → MeanWind v_lon/v_lat/v_lev).\n\nsource_ref: EarthSciData.jl@830435a065f27e99f10bba91107ca1730322cc6b:src/geosfp.jl:410\n\nUpstream GEOSFP(domain, domaininfo; name=:GEOSFP, stream=true, spatial_interp=:linear) creates an MTK System with:\n  - @parameters: lon/lat (rad) and lev (1) from pvars(domaininfo); t_ref (s)\n  - For every varname in every GEOSFPFileSet collection (A1/A3cld/A3dyn/A3mstC/A3mstE/I3),\n    one DataSetInterpolator and one observed equation via create_interp_equation (uses interp_unsafe)\n  - Coordinate mapping: lon/lat in radians (loadmetadata converts from degrees); lev=1..72\n  - Staggering: geosfp_staggering() returns:\n      A3dyn/U   → (true, false, false)  # x-staggered (lon edges)\n      A3dyn/V   → (false, true, false)  # y-staggered (lat edges)\n      A3dyn/OMEGA → (false, false, true)  # z-staggered (lev interfaces)\n      all others → (false, false, false) # cell-centered\n  - Extrapolation: OMEGA uses zero extrapolation (extrapolate_type=0.0); all others use Flat() (clamp)\n  - Hybrid pressure: P ~ P_unit * Ap(lev) + Bp(lev) * I3₊PS\n    where Ap/Bp are DataInterpolations.LinearInterpolation tables indexed 1:73\n    (lev=1 → surface ≈ PS, lev=73 → 1 Pa). Encoded as the top-level function_tables geosfp_Ap_pa (Pa) and geosfp_Bp (dimensionless); P is observed = table_lookup(geosfp_Ap_pa, lev) + table_lookup(geosfp_Bp, lev) * GEOSFP_I3.PS.\n  - Virtual temperature: Tv ~ T * (1 + 0.61 * QV); Tv_sfc ~ T2M * (1 + 0.61 * QV2M)\n  - Layer-mean virtual temp: Tv̄ ~ 0.5 * (Tv + Tv_sfc)\n  - Coordinate metrics (lat/lon domain only): δxδlon ~ lon2m * cos(lat); δyδlat ~ lat2meters\n  - discrete_events: build_interp_event fires at each file collection boundary to reload buffers\n  - metadata: Dict(CoupleType => GEOSFPCoupler, SysDomainInfo => domaininfo)\n  - couple2 with MeanWindCoupler: maps GEOSFP.A3dyn₊U/V/OMEGA → MeanWind v_lon/v_lat/v_lev\n\ngt-p3ep resolution: the @register_symbolic interp_unsafe pattern for all file-variable equations is replaced by the data_loaders §8 mechanism (GEOSFP_A1.*, GEOSFP_A3*.*, GEOSFP_I3.* references). The Ap/Bp hybrid coordinate tables — formerly the GEOSFP_hybrid_coefs (kind: lookup) data loader, a kind removed in the 0.6.0 hard break — are now the top-level function_tables geosfp_Ap_pa and geosfp_Bp, resolving the fixed-table lookup gap for P.\n\ngt-6ohw gap (DataInterpolations.derivative): δPδlev and δZδlev require the symbolic derivative of Ap(lev) and Bp(lev) with respect to lev (via DataInterpolations.derivative), which is not yet representable in the ESM expression language. These variables are omitted. When gt-6ohw is resolved:\n  δPδlev (Pa): d(P)/d(lev) = d(Ap(lev))/d(lev) + d(Bp(lev))/d(lev) * PS\n    For the linear interpolation with unit spacing: d(Ap)/d(lev) at integer lev n = Ap[n+1]-Ap[n]\n    The upstream code uses: expand_derivatives(Differential(lev)(P_unit * Ap(lev) + Bp(lev) * PS))\n  δZδlev (m): d(Z_agl)/d(lev) — requires Pmid = P_unit*Ap(lev+0.5)+Bp(lev+0.5)*PS (gt-p3ep(lookup)\n    with lev+0.5 offset) and derivatives of Ap/Bp at lev+0.5 (gt-6ohw). Both gaps must be resolved.\n\nZ_agl gap (gt-p3ep(lookup)): Z_agl = (Rd * Tv̄ / g) * log(PS / Pmid) where\n  Pmid = P_unit * Ap(lev+0.5) + Bp(lev+0.5) * PS\n  Evaluating Ap and Bp at the fractional level lev+0.5 is an offset-indexed lookup (gt-p3ep(lookup))\n  not yet representable in the ESM expression language. Z_agl is omitted; when gt-p3ep(lookup) is\n  resolved, add:\n    Pmid = table_lookup(geosfp_Ap_pa, lev+0.5) + table_lookup(geosfp_Bp, lev+0.5) * GEOSFP_I3.PS\n    Z_agl = (287.05 * Tv̄ / 9.80665) * log(I3₊PS / Pmid)\n\nUpstream test values at (-155.7°, 39.1°) for domain '4x5' (EarthSciData.jl test/geosfp_test.jl):\n  P at lev=[1,2,3,71,72,73]: [102340.38, 101572.77, 100805.17, 2.0, 1.5, 1.0] Pa\n  OMEGA at lev=[0.5,1,1.5,2,35,70,72.5]: [0.0, -0.00385, -0.00770, -0.00652, 1.12e-5, 0.0, 0.0] Pa/s\n  Z_agl at various levels: 63.38 m (lev=1.5) to 80132.64 m (lev=72.5)\n\nDomain notes: the default domain '0.25x0.3125' is the native GEOS-FP global grid. Regional and coarser domains (e.g. '4x5', '0.25x0.3125_NA', '2x2.5') change the URL prefix GEOS_{domain}/GEOS_FP/ and the filename suffix. The transformed domain in the filename replaces dots with nothing and underscores with dots: '0.25x0.3125_NA' → '025x03125.NA'. This ESM documents the default 0.25x0.3125 global domain."
      },
      "tolerance": {
        "rel": 1e-06
      },
      "variables": {
        "lon": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "rad",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Longitude of the model grid point (radians). Coupled to the simulation domain's longitude coordinate via param_to_var. Used for GEOSFP data spatial interpolation."
        },
        "lat": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "rad",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Latitude of the model grid point (radians). Coupled to the simulation domain's latitude coordinate via param_to_var. Used for GEOSFP data spatial interpolation."
        },
        "lev": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 1.0,
          "description": "Hybrid vertical level index (dimensionless, 1-based). lev=1 is the bottom interface (P≈PS, near-surface); lev=73 is the top interface (P≈1 Pa). Layer centers are at lev=1.5, 2.5, ..., 72.5. Interpolation within the Ap/Bp tables is linear with unit spacing."
        },
        "t_ref": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "s",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Reference epoch (seconds since the Julia DateTime epoch) from which the GEOS-FP file time axis is offset. Set from DomainInfo.get_tref(domaininfo) at construction time."
        },
        "t_interp_ref_I3": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "s",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "TIME INTERPOLATION (loader records_per_sample=2), I3 cadence. Simulation-clock time (s) of any cadence anchor of the I3 (instantaneous 3-hourly: T, QV, PS) collection — i.e. a time at which a fresh record lands, so the interpolation weight w_time_I3 is exactly 0 there. Together with dt_interp_I3 it locates the current time within its bracketing record pair WITHOUT the runtime injecting timestamps.\n\nGEOS-FP's collections are NOT co-phased, which is why this model carries THREE independent (ref, dt) pairs rather than era5_single.esm's single one: the native records sit at 00:00, 03:00, ... UTC The default assumes the run clock has t=0 at 00:00 UTC of the file's day; a runner whose t=0 is elsewhere must offset it."
        },
        "dt_interp_I3": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "s",
          "default": 10800.0,
          "description": "TIME INTERPOLATION: the I3 cadence step (s) between the two bracketing records — I3 is 3-hourly, so 10800. Must equal the EarthSciIO LoaderTemporal.frequency the provider brackets on, so this model's weight phase agrees with which two records the provider actually loaded."
        },
        "w_time_I3": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "TIME INTERPOLATION weight in [0,1) for the I3 cadence: the fractional position of the current simulation time t within its bracketing pair of I3 records, w = frac((t - t_interp_ref_I3)/dt_interp_I3). Because it reads the simulation clock `t` it is CONTINUOUS (per-step): w ramps 0->1 across each cadence interval and resets to 0 at the next record, so a consumer blending the two bracketing fields as (1 - w)*F0 + w*F1 varies smoothly between records instead of stepping.\n\nMirrors era5_single.esm's w_time; see t_interp_ref_I3 for why GEOS-FP needs three of these and ERA5 only one."
        },
        "t_interp_ref_A3": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "s",
          "default": 5400.0,
          "description": "TIME INTERPOLATION (loader records_per_sample=2), A3 cadence. Simulation-clock time (s) of any cadence anchor of the A3dyn/A3cld/A3mstC/A3mstE (3-hourly time-AVERAGED: U, V, OMEGA, RH, DTRAIN, ...) collection — i.e. a time at which a fresh record lands, so the interpolation weight w_time_A3 is exactly 0 there. Together with dt_interp_A3 it locates the current time within its bracketing record pair WITHOUT the runtime injecting timestamps.\n\nGEOS-FP's collections are NOT co-phased, which is why this model carries THREE independent (ref, dt) pairs rather than era5_single.esm's single one: the native records sit at 01:30, 04:30, ... UTC — the mid-points of the 3 h averaging windows The default assumes the run clock has t=0 at 00:00 UTC of the file's day; a runner whose t=0 is elsewhere must offset it."
        },
        "dt_interp_A3": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "s",
          "default": 10800.0,
          "description": "TIME INTERPOLATION: the A3 cadence step (s) between the two bracketing records — A3dyn/A3cld/A3mstC/A3mstE is 3-hourly, so 10800. Must equal the EarthSciIO LoaderTemporal.frequency the provider brackets on, so this model's weight phase agrees with which two records the provider actually loaded."
        },
        "w_time_A3": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "TIME INTERPOLATION weight in [0,1) for the A3 cadence: the fractional position of the current simulation time t within its bracketing pair of A3dyn/A3cld/A3mstC/A3mstE records, w = frac((t - t_interp_ref_A3)/dt_interp_A3). Because it reads the simulation clock `t` it is CONTINUOUS (per-step): w ramps 0->1 across each cadence interval and resets to 0 at the next record, so a consumer blending the two bracketing fields as (1 - w)*F0 + w*F1 varies smoothly between records instead of stepping.\n\nMirrors era5_single.esm's w_time; see t_interp_ref_A3 for why GEOS-FP needs three of these and ERA5 only one."
        },
        "t_interp_ref_A1": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "s",
          "default": 1800.0,
          "description": "TIME INTERPOLATION (loader records_per_sample=2), A1 cadence. Simulation-clock time (s) of any cadence anchor of the A1 (hourly time-AVERAGED: PBLH, T2M, U10M, SWGDN, ...) collection — i.e. a time at which a fresh record lands, so the interpolation weight w_time_A1 is exactly 0 there. Together with dt_interp_A1 it locates the current time within its bracketing record pair WITHOUT the runtime injecting timestamps.\n\nGEOS-FP's collections are NOT co-phased, which is why this model carries THREE independent (ref, dt) pairs rather than era5_single.esm's single one: the native records sit at 00:30, 01:30, ... UTC — the mid-points of the 1 h averaging windows The default assumes the run clock has t=0 at 00:00 UTC of the file's day; a runner whose t=0 is elsewhere must offset it."
        },
        "dt_interp_A1": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "s",
          "default": 3600.0,
          "description": "TIME INTERPOLATION: the A1 cadence step (s) between the two bracketing records — A1 is hourly, so 3600. Must equal the EarthSciIO LoaderTemporal.frequency the provider brackets on, so this model's weight phase agrees with which two records the provider actually loaded."
        },
        "w_time_A1": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "TIME INTERPOLATION weight in [0,1) for the A1 cadence: the fractional position of the current simulation time t within its bracketing pair of A1 records, w = frac((t - t_interp_ref_A1)/dt_interp_A1). Because it reads the simulation clock `t` it is CONTINUOUS (per-step): w ramps 0->1 across each cadence interval and resets to 0 at the next record, so a consumer blending the two bracketing fields as (1 - w)*F0 + w*F1 varies smoothly between records instead of stepping.\n\nMirrors era5_single.esm's w_time; see t_interp_ref_A1 for why GEOS-FP needs three of these and ERA5 only one."
        },
        "T": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K",
          "description": "Air temperature (K). 3-hourly instantaneous 3D field on the GEOS-FP hybrid pressure levels. Sourced from GEOSFP_I3.T. Used in virtual temperature calculation Tv = T * (1 + 0.61*QV)."
        },
        "QV": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/kg",
          "description": "Specific humidity of water vapor (kg/kg). 3-hourly instantaneous 3D field. Sourced from GEOSFP_I3.QV. Used in virtual temperature calculation."
        },
        "PS": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "Pa",
          "description": "Surface pressure (Pa). 3-hourly instantaneous 2D field (no lev dimension). Used in hybrid pressure calculation P = Ap[lev] + Bp[lev]*PS. Sourced from GEOSFP_I3.PS."
        },
        "T2M": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K",
          "description": "Air temperature at 2m above the displacement height (K). 1-hourly time-averaged 2D surface field. Used in near-surface virtual temperature Tv_sfc = T2M * (1 + 0.61*QV2M). Sourced from GEOSFP_A1.T2M."
        },
        "QV2M": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/kg",
          "description": "Specific humidity at 2m (kg/kg). 1-hourly time-averaged 2D surface field. Used in near-surface virtual temperature Tv_sfc. Sourced from GEOSFP_A1.QV2M."
        },
        "U10M": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m/s",
          "description": "Eastward wind at 10m above the displacement height (m/s). 1-hourly time-averaged 2D surface field. Sourced from GEOSFP_A1.U10M."
        },
        "V10M": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m/s",
          "description": "Northward wind at 10m above the displacement height (m/s). 1-hourly time-averaged 2D surface field. Sourced from GEOSFP_A1.V10M."
        },
        "PBLH": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "description": "Planetary boundary layer height (m). 1-hourly time-averaged 2D field. Sourced from GEOSFP_A1.PBLH."
        },
        "PRECTOT": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/m^2/s",
          "description": "Total precipitation rate (kg m⁻² s⁻¹). 1-hourly time-averaged 2D field (large-scale plus convective). Sourced from GEOSFP_A1.PRECTOT."
        },
        "PRECANV": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/m^2/s",
          "description": "Anvil precipitation rate (kg m⁻² s⁻¹). 1-hourly time-averaged 2D field. Sourced from GEOSFP_A1.PRECANV."
        },
        "SLP": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "Pa",
          "description": "Sea-level pressure (Pa). 1-hourly time-averaged 2D field. Sourced from GEOSFP_A1.SLP."
        },
        "TS": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K",
          "description": "Surface skin temperature (K). 1-hourly time-averaged 2D field. Sourced from GEOSFP_A1.TS."
        },
        "CLDTOT": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Total cloud fraction (dimensionless, 0–1). 1-hourly time-averaged 2D field. Sourced from GEOSFP_A1.CLDTOT."
        },
        "SWGDN": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "W/m^2",
          "description": "Incident shortwave flux at the ground (W m⁻²). 1-hourly time-averaged 2D field. Sourced from GEOSFP_A1.SWGDN."
        },
        "TROPP_H": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "Pa",
          "description": "Tropopause pressure using the thermal definition (Pa). 1-hourly time-averaged 2D field. Sourced from GEOSFP_A1.TROPP_H."
        },
        "FRSEAICE": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Sea ice area fraction (dimensionless, 0–1). 1-hourly time-averaged 2D field. Sourced from GEOSFP_A1.FRSEAICE."
        },
        "GWETTOP": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Topsoil moisture (volumetric, dimensionless). 1-hourly time-averaged 2D field. Sourced from GEOSFP_A1.GWETTOP."
        },
        "LAI": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Leaf area index (m² leaf per m² ground, dimensionless). 1-hourly time-averaged 2D field. Sourced from GEOSFP_A1.LAI."
        },
        "USTAR": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m/s",
          "description": "Surface friction velocity (m/s). 1-hourly time-averaged 2D field. Sourced from GEOSFP_A1.USTAR."
        },
        "Z0M": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "description": "Surface roughness length for momentum (m). 1-hourly time-averaged 2D field. Sourced from GEOSFP_A1.Z0M."
        },
        "U": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m/s",
          "description": "Eastward wind component (m/s). 3-hourly time-averaged 3D field. Cell-center staggered in y and z; x-edge-staggered (lon-edge aligned, de-staggered by runtime). Sourced from GEOSFP_A3dyn.U. Coupled to MeanWind.v_lon via GEOSFPCoupler/couple2. Clamp extrapolation."
        },
        "V": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m/s",
          "description": "Northward wind component (m/s). 3-hourly time-averaged 3D field. y-edge-staggered (lat-edge aligned, de-staggered by runtime). Sourced from GEOSFP_A3dyn.V. Coupled to MeanWind.v_lat via GEOSFPCoupler/couple2. Clamp extrapolation."
        },
        "OMEGA": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "Pa/s",
          "description": "Vertical pressure velocity (Pa/s). 3-hourly time-averaged 3D field. z-edge-staggered (lev-interface aligned, de-staggered by runtime). Sourced from GEOSFP_A3dyn.OMEGA. Coupled to MeanWind.v_lev via GEOSFPCoupler/couple2. Zero extrapolation (extrapolate_type=0.0) to prevent spurious vertical mass transport."
        },
        "RH": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Relative humidity with respect to liquid water (dimensionless, 0–1). 3-hourly time-averaged 3D field. Sourced from GEOSFP_A3dyn.RH. Clamp extrapolation."
        },
        "DTRAIN": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/m^2/s",
          "description": "Detrainment of cloud mass (kg m⁻² s⁻¹). 3-hourly time-averaged 3D field. Sourced from GEOSFP_A3dyn.DTRAIN. Clamp extrapolation."
        },
        "CLOUD": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "3D cloud fraction (dimensionless, 0–1). 3-hourly time-averaged 3D field. Sourced from GEOSFP_A3cld.CLOUD. Clamp extrapolation."
        },
        "QI": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/kg",
          "description": "Mass fraction of cloud ice water (kg/kg). 3-hourly time-averaged 3D field. Sourced from GEOSFP_A3cld.QI. Clamp extrapolation."
        },
        "QL": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/kg",
          "description": "Mass fraction of cloud liquid water (kg/kg). 3-hourly time-averaged 3D field. Sourced from GEOSFP_A3cld.QL. Clamp extrapolation."
        },
        "OPTDEPTH": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Grid-mean cloud optical depth at visible wavelengths (dimensionless). 3-hourly time-averaged 3D field. Sourced from GEOSFP_A3cld.OPTDEPTH. Clamp extrapolation."
        },
        "TAUCLI": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Optical thickness of convective ice cloud (dimensionless). 3-hourly time-averaged 3D field. Sourced from GEOSFP_A3cld.TAUCLI. Clamp extrapolation."
        },
        "TAUCLW": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "description": "Optical thickness of convective liquid cloud (dimensionless). 3-hourly time-averaged 3D field. Sourced from GEOSFP_A3cld.TAUCLW. Clamp extrapolation."
        },
        "CMFMC": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/m^2/s",
          "description": "Upward moist convective mass flux (kg m⁻² s⁻¹). 3-hourly time-averaged 3D field. Sourced from GEOSFP_A3mstC.CMFMC. Clamp extrapolation."
        },
        "DQRCU": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/kg/s",
          "description": "Convective rain production (kg kg⁻¹ s⁻¹). 3-hourly time-averaged 3D field. Sourced from GEOSFP_A3mstC.DQRCU. Clamp extrapolation."
        },
        "DQRLSAN": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/kg/s",
          "description": "Large-scale rain and snow production (kg kg⁻¹ s⁻¹). 3-hourly time-averaged 3D field. Sourced from GEOSFP_A3mstC.DQRLSAN. Clamp extrapolation."
        },
        "REEEVAP": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/kg/s",
          "description": "Evaporation of convective precipitation (kg kg⁻¹ s⁻¹). 3-hourly time-averaged 3D field. Sourced from GEOSFP_A3mstC.REEEVAP. Clamp extrapolation."
        },
        "CMFMC_OCE": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/m^2/s",
          "description": "Downward moist convective mass flux from ocean (kg m⁻² s⁻¹). 3-hourly time-averaged 3D field. Sourced from GEOSFP_A3mstE.CMFMC_OCE. Clamp extrapolation."
        },
        "PFICU": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/m^2/s",
          "description": "Downward flux of ice mass from convection (kg m⁻² s⁻¹). 3-hourly time-averaged 3D field. Sourced from GEOSFP_A3mstE.PFICU. Clamp extrapolation."
        },
        "PFILSAN": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/m^2/s",
          "description": "Downward flux of ice mass from large-scale precipitation and snowfall (kg m⁻² s⁻¹). 3-hourly time-averaged 3D field. Sourced from GEOSFP_A3mstE.PFILSAN. Clamp extrapolation."
        },
        "PFLCU": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/m^2/s",
          "description": "Downward flux of liquid mass from convection (kg m⁻² s⁻¹). 3-hourly time-averaged 3D field. Sourced from GEOSFP_A3mstE.PFLCU. Clamp extrapolation."
        },
        "PFLLSAN": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/m^2/s",
          "description": "Downward flux of liquid mass from large-scale precipitation and snowfall (kg m⁻² s⁻¹). 3-hourly time-averaged 3D field. Sourced from GEOSFP_A3mstE.PFLLSAN. Clamp extrapolation."
        },
        "P": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "Pa",
          "description": "Atmospheric pressure at hybrid level lev (Pa): P = Ap(lev) + Bp(lev)*PS. Ap [Pa] and Bp [dimensionless] are the GEOS-FP 72-level (73-edge) hybrid sigma-pressure coefficients, evaluated at the 1-based level index lev by piecewise-linear interpolation (interp.linear over the integer level axis 1..73; lev=1 -> surface ~ PS, lev=73 -> ~1 Pa). PS is the surface pressure from the GEOSFP_I3 loader subsystem. Uses interp.linear with inline const coefficient arrays (the tree-walk-native form, as fastjx.esm does) rather than a table_lookup over top-level function_tables, because the runtime evaluator does not lower/evaluate table_lookup."
        },
        "Tv": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K",
          "description": "Virtual temperature at pressure level (K). Tv = T × (1 + 0.61 × QV), where T is air temperature and QV is specific humidity. Used in geopotential height calculation Z_agl (which is omitted due to gt-p3ep(lookup); see reference.notes)."
        },
        "Tv_sfc": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K",
          "description": "Near-surface virtual temperature at 2m (K). Tv_sfc = T2M × (1 + 0.61 × QV2M). Used in layer-mean virtual temperature Tv̄."
        },
        "Tv_bar": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "K",
          "description": "Layer-mean virtual temperature (K). Tv̄ = 0.5 × (Tv + Tv_sfc). Used in Z_agl hypsometric height calculation (omitted; see reference.notes)."
        },
        "δxδlon": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m/rad",
          "description": "Coordinate metric: x-distance per unit longitude (m rad⁻¹). δxδlon = lon2m × cos(lat) where lon2m = 40075×10³/(2π) ≈ 6378134.3 m rad⁻¹. Emitted only in lat/lon coordinate domains."
        },
        "δyδlat": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m/rad",
          "description": "Coordinate metric: y-distance per unit latitude (m rad⁻¹). δyδlat = lat2meters = 111.32×10³×(180/π) ≈ 6378166.0 m rad⁻¹. Constant. Emitted only in lat/lon coordinate domains."
        }
      },
